# What EAS Build does NOT need to upload.
#
# The app lives in native/, but this repository also holds the website, the
# Qur'an assets, the worker and the admin pages. EAS archives from the git root
# — the build machine unpacks it and then looks for the app at native/ — so
# without this it uploads all 800MB of it, compressed to 178MB, every single
# build.
#
# When this file exists EAS uses it INSTEAD of .gitignore, so anything that must
# not be uploaded has to be listed here even if .gitignore already covers it.
# That is why node_modules and the generated native projects appear below.
#
# Everything is anchored with a leading slash on purpose, and the root files are
# named rather than matched with a wildcard. An unanchored `assets/` would also
# match native/assets/, which holds the app icon and the fonts, and a `*.png`
# that behaved differently than expected would quietly drop the icon. Naming
# them costs a few lines and removes the question. That is not a
# hypothetical: an unanchored `package.json` in .gitignore hid
# native/package.json from the archiver and failed a build in 37 seconds with
# "package.json does not exist in /Users/expo/workingdir/build/native".

# Dependencies and generated native projects — rebuilt on the build machine.
node_modules/
/native/ios/
/native/android/
/native/.expo/
/native/dist/

# Screenshot and comparison output from the local tooling.
/native/ios-shots/
/native/store-shots/
/native/.darkshots/
/native/.compare/

# The website and its assets. None of it is compiled into the app.
/quran/
/data/
/db/
/lang/
/fonts/
/assets/
/portal/
/push/
/worker/
/store/
/scripts/
/docs/
/.well-known/
/Taiyabah-Mosque-App/
/admin.html
/delete-data.html
/index.html
/privacy.html
/apple-touch-icon.png
/icon-1024.png
/icon-192.png
/icon-512.png
/logo.svg
/manifest.webmanifest
/sw.js
/CNAME
/.nojekyll
/twa-manifest.json

# Repository documentation.
/README.md
/ROADMAP.md
/STATUS.md
/LICENSE.md
